    "body": "## ADR-KERNEL-08: owner acceptance, verified chronology, evidence scope (documentation only)\n\n**Do not merge on my account: this PR is for the owner's review.** No code, test, harness or policy changed (8 `.md` files). Baseline: `main` `2491ae4`.\n\n### Decisions recorded\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| **§8.1 item 1** | **ACCEPTED by the owner, Nov 1, 2026**, *after* PR #93 merged (03:23:47Z). Recorded on the owner's statement (it was given in conversation; GitHub doesn't hold it). Scope and non-claims are explicit. The defect the review found was fixed in `0c16cd3`, verified: ancestor of `main`; parent's harness byte-identical to the file reviewed; harness unchanged since. |\n| §8.1 item 2 | PERFORMED Oct 31, 2026 (19:17:56Z), with its limits |\n| §8.1 item 3 | COMPLETED (twice: over `16d663a`, then `ed3d141`) |\n| ADR status | **IMPLEMENTED, not FINAL.** Searched the ADR, the index, the other ADRs and `PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS.md`: **no finalization criteria are defined anywhere**, so none is met or invented. |\n| CTX-AUTH-002 | CLOSED (qualified), unchanged |\n| **CTX-AUTH-001b** | **OPEN, unchanged**. REM-004, REM-002, DEBT-025 untouched. |\n\n### A correction of my own earlier records\nRecords I wrote for the Nov 1 events (PR #93 merge, IMPLEMENTED, CTX-AUTH-002 closure) were dated **Oct 31**. GitHub: PR #93 `merged_at` **2026-11-01T03:23:47Z**, PR #106 **2026-11-01T12:31:28Z**. **14 occurrences corrected to Nov 1** (itemised in ADR §8.3.6; git history keeps the originals). The 6 accurate Oct 31 labels (experiment, `099a238`, the notes written with `396e374`) are untouched. A UTC chronology table is in §8.3.2.\n\n### Evidence scope (ADR §8.3.4)\n- One local model (`Ollama(llama3)`). **Harness-defined `ESCALATED=0` is not a count of Plan Compiler `GovernanceVerdict.ESCALATE`**; the harness imports only `intent`, `planner`, `unified_memory` and the prompt cache, and never calls compile or execute (checked in the code).\n- **R3 = 10 of 30 trials** (10 prompts x 3), a fallback-selection outcome: not a task-failure rate, user-visible cost unassessed, and **no valid baseline** (the ADR's own R6 says the Oct 8/9 runs are not acceptance evidence; I qualified my earlier §8.2 sentence that had cited their 10%/30%).\n- **Not repaired by inference:** `git_commit=unknown` (tested revision is inferred from the harness hash and byte-identical interpreter files) and the exit status (derived from the code path, not observed).\n- `out.json` is **not published**. Its sha256 is documented; I re-hashed the supplied file (equal), but that hash was originally computed by me, so it is **not an independent attestation**.\n\n### R1 re-audited against live `main`\n`build_capability_discovery_request()` and `build_planner_request()`, the only readers of `semantic_description` and the category hint, have **no production call site**; `Orchestrator.handle()` builds `PlannerRequest` directly. R1 is stated as the brief specified: *latent integration risk, not demonstrated active impact*, with the caveat that this is a static search. Two things the brief did not anticipate, both checked: `content_anchor.py`'s `\"novel\": \"story\"` is a raw-text token map, not a label consumer; and the compiler's clarification escalation uses `plan.confidence`, which `_estimate_confidence()` derives from capability-match relevance and **not** from goal confidence.\n\n### K4.2 documents (additive, dated, bodies unchanged)\nThe completion report's `_extract_constraints (uses semantic_description)` was **accurate when written** (the code read it until the Oct 5 remediation, `efac585`, which reached `main` with PR #93), so it is a *supersession* note, not \"was wrong\". The contract-evolution spec's **[FACT]** that no inline `PlannerRequest`/`CapabilityDiscoveryRequest` construction exists was already contradicted by `orchestrator.py` (Aug 8, before the spec's Aug 14) and by `check_drift.py` DRIFT-14; noted likewise.\n\n### Validation actually run\n`scripts/check_drift.py`: exit 0, 30 PASS, 0 FAIL. Docs-related tests (`-k \"adr or drift or doc or known_issues or current_state or index\"`): 90 passed. Approved ADR §§1-8.1 asserted byte-identical before and after. Changed paths NUL-checked: all `.md`; no untracked files. Added lines scanned: 0 credential-like strings, no non-loopback URLs, no raw record data. Markdown tables/fences checked. Every embedded commit, timestamp and count recomputed from git/GitHub. **Not run:** a Markdown link checker or formatter (none configured in the repo that I found).\n\n### For the reviewer\n- **Merge-order conflicts are likely** at the top of `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` / `CURRENT_STATE.md`: 7 open branches (incl. DEBT-025 #94 and draft #107) also add entries there.\n- The owner did not say whether the acceptance came before or after PR #106's merge, so that order is **not recorded** (§8.3.2).\n- ADR §8.1 said item 1 was required *before* promotion; the acceptance post-dates it. Recorded as it happened, not repaired.\n",
