    "body": "## Purpose\n\nReconcile the current debt/status record, branch ownership, and repository entry-point README against live GitHub state without performing product remediation or making unresolved owner decisions.\n\n**Snapshot baseline:** `main` @ `2491ae469edd6ef1267a14604c4f8f40d698f7ea` (PR #106).\n\n## Files\n\n- `README.md`: replaces the stale August 2026 overview with a November 2 status snapshot and a deeper architecture/vision guide. It distinguishes current kernel and K4.2 behavior from future architecture; explains the post-freeze C-MoE role and boundaries; covers WorkGraph, goal preservation, user task mutation, scoped memory, reality grounding, adaptive effort, and abstention; separates Verification, Reflection, Evaluation, and Adaptive Learning; adds Studio/operator-plane and AGI research directions; and documents OCBrain's system-wide adaptability.\n- `KNOWN_ISSUES.md`: dated current snapshot; corrects FZ-01/FZ-02/FZ-06/FZ-07 status wording, repairs the truncated DEBT-018 row, records the C-plus decision for DEBT-043 as selected-but-not-implemented, and records PR #94 as an unmerged DEBT-025 candidate rather than a closure.\n- `CURRENT_STATE.md`: matching current-state entry and explicit distinction between main, open PRs and preserved branches.\n- `docs/engineering/DEBT_BRANCH_OWNERSHIP_REGISTER_2026-11-02.md`: complete 111-ref branch inventory, all 20 open PRs, three open non-PR issues, debt-to-PR mapping, stale/competing branches and ownership gaps.\n\n## Strategic boundaries recorded in README\n\n- **Kernel first:** the current freeze blockers and reliability/authority gaps take priority. No freeze-ready or production-ready claim is made.\n- **C-MoE is post-Kernel-v1.0-freeze:** it is a system-level Cognitive Mixture of Experts, not neural MoE and not merely a multi-LLM router. It routes heterogeneous capabilities/experts, manages WorkGraph realization and outcome feedback, and optimizes for reaching the authorized goal.\n- **C-MoE authority is bounded:** it proposes; GovernanceKernel authorizes. Planner, runtime, verification, memory, and Studio keep distinct responsibilities.\n- **Verification / Critic / Evidence is a separate assurance system:** the current Phase C contracts remain unmerged and are not production integration.\n- **AGI is a long-term ambition:** README treats it as a system-level aspiration requiring generalization, long-horizon coherence, grounded action, independent assurance, governed learning, and user sovereignty. It expressly does not claim achieved AGI, consciousness, or an approved AGI milestone.\n- **Adaptability is cross-cutting, not synonymous with C-MoE:** README covers deployment/provider variability, Computational Levels (LOW/MEDIUM/HIGH/MAX), Resource Policy and Resource Envelope derivation, task/context/risk-aware allocations, operational health, goal mutation, and bounded resource-aware execution.\n- **Adaptability is not overstated:** README identifies existing lower-level primitives (latency-adaptive concurrency, provider failure/cooldown behavior, throughput observations, bounded time budgets), while clearly stating that a wired Computational Level selector, Resource Policy Engine, Resource Envelope, and complete token/cost/reasoning-effort/expert-count controls are not yet implemented. It also records that the Workspace domain model file contains candidate types but is non-conformant, unwired and untested per the canonical Workspace architecture.\n- **Resource policy remains independent of C-MoE:** the system can develop controlled resource adaptation separately; C-MoE may later provide complexity analysis or recommendations but does not own policy or enforcement.\n- **Local-first remains foundational:** a local LLM path is first-class; hosted providers and Expert Mesh are optional adapters. Selectable effort levels are target policy, not a claim of current implementation.\n- **Studio is an operator/control plane:** it should project authoritative runtime events and snapshots, not create a parallel execution state.\n\nThe README links to the underlying Kernel Completion, C-MoE, Reality-Grounding, Verification, Architecture Evolution, Adaptive Scaling, Workspace Architecture, and Future Research documents, while explicitly labeling research as research.\n\n## Ownership treatment\n\nGitHub showed no assignees on the 19 pre-existing open PRs; the reconciliation PR is also unassigned. PR authorship and last commit authorship are provenance only, not implementation ownership. Where there is no explicit assignment, the implementation owner is recorded as **UNASSIGNED**. No individual has been assigned by this PR.\n\n## Preserved boundaries\n\n- Documentation only: no product code, tests, CI, runtime contracts or ADRs changed.\n- No debt is closed by the documentation update.\n- No merge, rebase, branch deletion, issue closure or assignee mutation was performed.\n- PR #94 remains unmerged and its description says merge was not requested.\n- PR #107 remains diagnostic-only / NOT FOR MERGE.\n- G4 remains OPEN / High / freeze-blocking; D1-D11 remain OPEN; no implementation is authorized.\n- CTX-AUTH-002 remains CLOSED (qualified); CTX-AUTH-001b remains OPEN.\n- FZ-02 router cleanup (#104) is explicitly not represented as end-to-end cancellation.\n- Branch-protection state could not be independently re-read by this connector (403); PR #87's `enforce_admins=true` claim is marked as requiring fresh verification.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Re-read live `main`, the branch inventory, open PRs, recent closed PRs and open non-PR issues.\n- Confirmed the exact current-main base and a documentation-only diff of four paths: `README.md`, `CURRENT_STATE.md`, `KNOWN_ISSUES.md`, and the ownership register.\n- Confirmed README syntax uses real Markdown code spans/fences and checked its linked architecture and research files on the branch.\n- The PR remains **DRAFT** pending maintainer review. CI success and this reconciliation do not authorize merging.",
