    "body": "**DRAFT — DO NOT MERGE. Diagnostic CI evidence only.**\n\nBatch 1A of the Kernel v1.0 freeze remediation (R-1 / `GATE-CI-ALLOWLIST`). Posture remains `NOT_FREEZE_READY`.\n\n**Review status (preserved):** the original Batch 1 commit `667cb94` received an independent review with disposition **NOT APPROVED FOR MERGE**. That attestation stands and is *not* superseded by this PR. This PR contains `667cb94` unchanged plus one hardening commit on top; it has **not** been independently reviewed. Opening it is not merge approval.\n\n**What this PR is for:** to run the real CI workflow once with the structured report plugin in **diagnostic mode**. The shipped signature policy is `PROPOSED`, so it excuses **no** failure: any of the 34 listed tests that fails in CI stays red, and its exception chain is printed by the gate and uploaded in the `pytest-output` artifact (`ci-gate-report.json`). Those real chains are the evidence needed to decide the failure-signature policy (open owner question Q3). **No policy is accepted here.**\n\n**Addresses the review findings:** exception type is matched (not just message substrings) with a deny list; PROPOSED/REVOKED policies cannot excuse failures; non-strict XPASS no longer counts as an ordinary pass; report schema 2 with collection inventory, per-test terminal-outcome and counts reconciliation; credential redaction in the uploaded report; D10/R-1 documentation reconciled (R-1 stays OPEN).\n\n**Not changed:** the 34 allowlist entries (content and order verified), the strict ADR-KERNEL-07 D-4 xfail, `scripts/check_drift.py`, `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (vs 667cb94), the legacy text path. PR #91 and DEBT-012 are tracked separately.\n\n**Known/expected:** the `drift-and-ownership` job may flag this branch name as not being a declared packet branch; that is unrelated to the gate change. Local verification only so far — see the Batch 1A report on `audit/freeze-remediation-batch0-oct2026`.\n",
    "closed_by": null,
