    "draft": false,
    "pull_request": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pulls/103",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/103",
      "diff_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/103.diff",
      "patch_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/103.patch",
      "merged_at": null
    },
    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds a standalone, proposed OCBrain v2 cognitive architecture and roadmap:\n\n- `docs/architecture/OCBRAIN_V2_UNIFIED_COGNITIVE_RUNTIME_ROADMAP.md`\n\nThis is a **documentation-only architecture proposal**. It does not replace or edit `IMPLEMENTATION_ROADMAP.md`, change the current approved v1.0 architecture, alter completed K4.2 work, or authorize implementation.\n\n## Why this proposal exists\n\nThe recent architecture discussion identified that skill adaptability makes Planning and C-MoE increasingly interdependent. Skill discovery, transfer, adaptation and composition can change the task decomposition itself; expert availability and actual execution outcomes can force strategy changes. Keeping Planner and C-MoE as separate top-level cognitive authorities would create repeated bidirectional handoffs, duplicated context, plan/skill version synchronization, stale assumptions and unclear disagreement/recovery ownership.\n\nThe proposal therefore investigates a **unified C-MoE Cognitive Runtime** in which the existing Planner becomes the foundation of an internal Planning Engine alongside Skill Intelligence, Expert Intelligence, Adaptive Strategy/Orchestration and a shared Cognitive Workspace.\n\nThe Planner is not replaced or rewritten now. K4.2 remains complete and intact; its implementation, contracts, interfaces, events and tests are to be reused and evolved when C-MoE is eventually implemented.\n\n## Important architectural safeguards included\n\n- C-MoE remains a Kernel-managed cognitive runtime, not a second Kernel.\n- GovernanceKernel retains authorization; UnifiedMemory retains persistence; WorkflowRuntime/ExecutionRuntime retain actual workflow and execution state.\n- The C-MoE WorkGraph is explicitly distinguished from Kernel-authoritative workflow/node state.\n- Plan Compilation and its governance gate remain the route from a cognitive strategy to executable Kernel work.\n- Skills are procedural methods, not experts, capabilities or tools; Skill Registry/Runtime remain supporting infrastructure, not another autonomous intelligence subsystem.\n- Skill transfer, composition, missing-skill versus missing-capability handling, skill versioning and governed SkillCandidate lifecycle are specified.\n- Existing BaseSkill infrastructure is treated as a starting point, not a hardened sandbox.\n- Independent Verification, Reflection and governed Learning retain their boundaries.\n- The proposal explicitly records that the approved Architecture Evolution Directive v1.0 must be formally superseded on the relevant future ownership boundary before v2 implementation.\n- It includes a phased roadmap, research comparison of separated versus unified designs, measurable evaluation criteria, migration rules, open decisions and implementation gates.\n\n## Integration strategy\n\nThis branch was created from `main` at `16d663ac8449965f774033da46d5063506a772a7` and contains one new documentation file only.\n\nPer the owner's explicit integration strategy, **keep this PR open and merge it last**, after the currently active v1.x/Kernel PRs that affect its baseline have been reconciled. Before merging, fetch the then-current `main`, re-check the source claims, update any stale statuses or links, and resolve any new architectural conflicts explicitly.\n\nMerging this document would add a proposal to the repository; it would **not** ratify OCBrain v2 or authorize code changes. Ratification and implementation authorization require a separate owner decision/ADR.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Fetched the committed file back from the branch and checked its metadata and required sections.\n- Compared branch against the current `main` at creation: one commit ahead, zero behind.\n- Diff contains exactly one added file, no code changes.\n- No tests were run because this PR changes documentation only.\n\n## Review focus\n\nPlease review the decision rationale, authority matrix, K4.2 preservation, WorkGraph/WorkflowRuntime boundary, Skill Runtime prerequisites, phased dependencies and the explicit v1.0 directive-supersession requirement.",
    "closed_by": null,
