    "body": "## DEBT-014 — consolidated canonical fix\n\nThis PR consolidates the work previously split across PRs #98–#101 into one review target, based directly on current `main` at `16d663ac8449965f774033da46d5063506a772a7`.\n\n### Scope\n- Extend DRIFT-10 to inspect `core/cognitive/learning.py`, while keeping DRIFT-05 unchanged.\n- Preserve only the structurally verified top-level `validation_gate()` governance call as the explicit exception.\n- Enforce the exception's result flow, fail-closed verdict handling, trusted governance imports and policy bindings, canonical action-type mapping, and guarded persistence path.\n- Only an explicit `GovernanceVerdict.APPROVE` permits the Evolution-tier write; unknown/future verdicts are rejected.\n- Include the regression tests and update `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` to remove DEBT-014 from the active register with the exact verification evidence and the bounded-AST limitation.\n\n### Reconciliation fixes\n- Distinguish reads of frozen scalar/tuple policy constants (for example `LearningTier.LEARNING` and `ContentDomain.ALL`) from aliases of class objects or references to mutable policy internals.\n- The indirect-mutation fixture includes both alias creation and subsequent mutation.\n- The global-result fixture uses the actual `VALID_LEARNING_PY` signature.\n- The tier/domain mapping fixture matches the source's quote style and asserts its anchor exists before mutation.\n- Positive regressions cover legitimate scalar, tuple, and conditional reads of frozen policy constants.\n\n### Verification\nThe earlier #101 head failed with 4 test failures and two DRIFT-10 false positives. These were traced and corrected.\n- CI run #434 on code head `76f2fc26115306691e7b7f560b5999d542248d23`: both jobs passed; pytest reported `2235 passed, 14 skipped, 1 xfailed, 2 warnings`, exit code 0.\n- The register-only follow-up commit `74e6f0d6db1d3e68588e03ad3ee986fe1b088a84` adds the DEBT-014 resolution record to this PR. The final CI run for this five-file, seven-commit head is required before merge.\n\nThe branch is seven commits ahead of current `main`, zero behind. PRs #98–#101 are superseded; this is the sole canonical open review target.",
