    },
    "body": "## DEBT-025: default-on authentication boundary for the HTTP API (A1 ACCEPTED), review remediation applied\n\n**Owner decision A1: ACCEPTED (Oct 28, 2026).** Authentication is required by default for every route except a pinned public allowlist; `/health` stays protected; the explicit, auditable opt-out is retained; loopback binding alone is not an adequate security boundary.\n**DEBT-025 stays OPEN**: authentication is not authorisation, and control-plane governance is unresolved (see \"Still open\").\n**Merge status: NOT requested.** Merging is the owner's call.\n\n**Base:** `main` `2491ae4` (includes PRs #89, #95/#96, #97, #104, #93 and #106). **Head (exact):** `c50caa9e4f9f8efe15f9e796857f45a4b34d6e25`. Review baseline `8552ca6e625fb9a54d0bb7d995284057d15fb7ea`; the diff between them is two files (`interface/auth.py`, `tests/test_api_auth_boundary.py`) and nothing else. 0 commits behind `main`, merged cleanly (the only overlapping file is `KNOWN_ISSUES.md`, different rows; DEBT-019's row is byte-identical to `main`).\nFull write-up: `docs/reports/api-exposure-and-auth-boundary-oct2026.md` (revised; it now lists three statements from its first version that review showed were wrong).\n\n## Latest checkpoint: two corrections from the review of `8552ca6` (now `c50caa9`)\nBoth were reproduced on the pushed head before being fixed.\n| Defect | Reproduced how | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Rejected responses carried none of the security headers** | 200 had all four; 401, 400 (foreign Host) and 503 had none: authentication is the outermost layer, so a rejection never reaches `SecurityHeadersMiddleware` | `_reject()` adds the same set; authentication stays outermost. Live: the 401 and the 400 now show the CSP and the other three |\n| **`ocbrain token --rotate` before the first start left the frozen per-user directory `0755`** | frozen-install simulation, umask 022: rotate-first gave dir `0755`, first-start gave `0700`; no test covered rotate-first | one helper (`_ensure_token_dir`) creates the directory for both paths: the frozen default is `0700`; an existing directory is **never** chmod-ed; a directory chosen with `OCBRAIN_API_TOKEN_FILE` keeps the default mode |\n\nAgainst `8552ca6` the six behavioural regression tests fail; two more pin behaviour that must not change (existing directory untouched, override path keeps default mode) and pass on both.\n\n## What the Oct 30 review found, and what changed (owner-authorised plan, Oct 31)\n| Finding (severity as I judged it) | Reproduced how | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Tray put the token on the browser's command line** (merge-blocking) | A stub launcher received `…#token=…`; an unprivileged uid read the whole token from `/proc/<pid>/cmdline` while the 0600 file was denied to it | The tray URL carries no token. The page asks once per tab; `ocbrain token --show` prints it. A one-time-code scheme was rejected: a local attacker could win the race to redeem it. |\n| **Opt-out auditable only once** (merge-blocking) | config hot-toggle disable, enable, disable gave 1 WARNING and nothing on re-enable | Every transition is logged and emitted (`api.auth_disabled`, new `api.auth_enabled`) |\n| **`Host` header not validated** (merge-blocking) | `Host: evil.example` got 200 for `/`, assets and the schema (DNS-rebinding route to the shell and its prompt) | Required mode accepts only `localhost`/`127.0.0.1`/`::1` plus `OCBRAIN_API_ALLOWED_HOSTS` / `global.api_allowed_hosts`; checked before the public allowlist |\n| **Public `/docs` and `/redoc` loaded CDN scripts into the UI's origin** (merge-blocking decision) | page source: `cdn.jsdelivr.net` | Docs UIs disabled (decision **made under the authorisation, reversible**: disable rather than self-host). `/openapi.json` now needs the token. Public = `GET /` and `/static/*` only. |\n| **Allowlist vs router path under `--root-path`** (regression) | pristine `main`: `/` 200; PR: 401 | Gate uses the router's root-path-stripped path |\n| **Frozen `--onefile` builds** (release-blocking) | PyInstaller build run twice: a new token in a different `_MEI…` dir each start | Per-user token location (`%LOCALAPPDATA%\\OCBrain`, `~/Library/Application Support/OCBrain`, `$XDG_DATA_HOME/ocbrain`), 0700 directory |\n| **Windows ACL not set** (release-blocking) | by reading; nothing could be validated on Linux | ACL restricted via `icacls` on create/load/rotate and checked as SDDL; validated by the new `token-acl-windows` job on a real Windows runner. **That job failed first and changed the design**, see below |\n| No revocation without a restart | file replaced or deleted while running: old token still 200 | The token file is re-checked on every request (one `stat`); `ocbrain token --rotate` or deleting the file revokes at once |\n| Wrong token typed into the prompt: modal every 5 s | 5 prompts in 21 s in a real browser | One prompt, then a 30 s quiet period, and the bad token is forgotten |\n| Unthrottled denial logging | 6000 requests wrote 6000 lines (456 KB) | At most 20 logged per 10 s plus a suppressed-count summary; **every request is still rejected** |\n| `chmod` followed a symlinked token file | by reading | A symlink to a loose file is refused, not chmod-ed through |\n| No security headers | by reading | CSP with no external origin, `nosniff`, `DENY`, `no-referrer` |\n| Install banners and `/debug` docstring said \"visit in your browser\" / `/docs` | by reading | They say how to get the token |\n\n**Two things I had to change that you did not ask for, because the fix depended on them:**\n1. `ocbrain token` must work in *both* install types. In a packaged install the binary named `ocbrain` **is the server** (`main.py`), in a pip install it is the click CLI. The command is implemented once (`interface/token_cli.py`) and reachable from both; `main.py` answers `token` before importing anything heavy.\n2. **Pre-existing CLI bug, minimally fixed:** under click 8.5 the group's optional `QUERY` argument swallowed the first word, so `ocbrain status` posted the text \"status\" to `/query` and `ocbrain train` never ran. A known subcommand name now wins; free text, `-m`, and piped input behave as before (all covered by tests).\n\n## Behaviour changes to know about\n- `/docs`, `/redoc` and the OpenAPI UI are gone; `/openapi.json` needs the token.\n- Required mode rejects requests whose `Host` is not an allowed name (400). Proxied deployments must set `OCBRAIN_API_ALLOWED_HOSTS`. The explicit opt-out does not apply this check.\n- The tray no longer opens the UI with a token; the page prompts once per tab.\n- Monitors that call `/health` need the bearer token.\n\n## Exact-head verification\nLinux gates were run on the exact head `c50caa9…` (`CI=true`, Python 3.12.3, `chromadb==0.5.3`). The Windows job result below is from `3300f93`; `interface/auth.py` changed since only in `_reject()` and the directory helper, neither of which the Windows ACL logic touches, and the job re-runs on this head: see its check.\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Full suite | **2372 passed, 1 xfailed, 0 failed** (baseline `main` `2491ae4`, same command: 2184 passed; +188) |\n| `scripts/check_drift.py` | no FAIL (15 checks) |\n| FastAPI 0.111.0 / Starlette 0.37.2 (the declared floor): boundary + Node tests | 188 passed (the full suite ran at the latest FastAPI/Starlette) |\n| 24 named security suites (`security`, `disclosure`, `auth`, `export`, `distill`, `import`, `sandbox`, `traversal`, `containment`) | 488 passed |\n| Mutation review: 38 mutants aimed at the new behaviour (Host, root-path, transitions, revocation, throttle, symlink, frozen path, Windows ACL logic, token-on-command-line, CLI routing, headers on rejections, rotate-first directory, docs, `main.py` hook, …) | **38/38 killed** |\n| Real browser (headless Chromium 153, **Linux**), harness outside the repo | 23/23: token-free tray URL then exactly one prompt; fragment adoption still works and is stripped; `sessionStorage` only; no CSP violation; SSE through the middleware; settings page; cross-origin page blocked at preflight; wrong token = one prompt in 21 s |\n| Live uvicorn probes | Host `evil.example`, `localhost.evil.example`, `192.168.1.5` all 400 even with a valid token; `localhost`/`127.0.0.1`/`[::1]` 200; allowed name via env 200; `/docs`,`/redoc` 401 then 404 with a token; `ocbrain token --rotate` revoked the old token on the running process (no restart), mode 600, no stray files; deleting the file revoked it; `status` hit `GET /status` (0 `POST /query`); missing token prints a clear message; 6000 unauthenticated requests in 18.0 s: all 401, log 456 KB → 3.7 KB (22 lines), server still serving; 401 and 400 responses carry the CSP, `nosniff`, `DENY` and `no-referrer`; `--root-path /ocb`: `/` and `/static` 200 as on `main`; opt-out toggle logged 2 disables and 1 re-enable; token value in the server log: 0 |\n| `main.py token --show` (packaged-binary path) | prints the token in 0.08 s; it returned immediately instead of running a server |\n| Frozen `--onefile` build (**Linux**) | fresh HOME, umask 022: **rotate first** gives dir 700 / file 600 and a later normal start and a separate `show` process both see the rotated token; first-start twice gives the same token, a separate process prints it, dir 700, file 600, nothing written under `_MEI…` |\n| CI on `8552ca6` (previous head) | `tests`, `drift-and-ownership`, CodeQL, both Analyze jobs, **`token-acl-windows`**: success; `mergeable_state` clean. CI on `c50caa9`: see this PR's checks. |\n\n### Windows (the part I could not validate from Linux)\nThe `token-acl-windows` job runs the real `icacls` on `windows-latest`. **Its first run failed, and the failure was the finding:**\n- A new file on that runner already has *explicit* `SYSTEM`, `BUILTIN\\Administrators` and `OWNER RIGHTS` entries, so my \"exactly one entry\" rule (written from Linux, and in the first version of the report) was unattainable; `/inheritance:r` removes nothing from them.\n- `/grant:r` alone also leaves any other explicit entry: an added `Everyone` entry survived, so my \"loosened ACLs are repaired\" claim was false too.\n- Changed: the recipe is `/reset` → `/inheritance:r` → `/grant:r *<SID>:(F)`, and the invariant is **no principal other than the current user, SYSTEM, Administrators and OWNER RIGHTS has an allow entry**, read as SDDL (SIDs, language-independent).\n- Result at `3300f93`: passes. New file: no broad principal in the listing, SDDL trustees = the user only (printed `LA`, the built-in Administrator alias); a deliberately added `Everyone`+`Users` read grant was present before and gone after the next load, token unchanged; rotation stayed private and left no temp file; the frozen-build default under `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\OCBrain` was created private.\n- **Limits of that evidence:** one runner, running as the built-in Administrator (elevated); English display names; it lists ACL entries and does not attempt a read as a second account. Not tried: a standard (non-admin) user, a domain account, another display language, a non-NTFS volume. macOS and a frozen build on Windows/macOS were not run. The unit tests stub `icacls` and prove logic only.\n\nEvidence labels: the Node live-server test (`tests/test_web_auth_js.py`, fails in CI if Node is missing) is **not** browser evidence; the browser run is Linux/Chromium only and not part of CI; everything POSIX proves nothing about NTFS.\n\n## Still open (not closed by this PR)\n- **Authenticated-but-unauthorized control-plane operations.** `/update/*`, `PUT /config` (including the mutable `global.ollama_host` and `global.web_ui_port`), `/import`, `/export`, `/distill`, `/rollback`, `/modules/new`, `/evolve/plan`, `/train/*` have no `GovernanceKernel` evaluation. **Open.**\n- **Durable auth events.** `api.auth_denied`/`api.auth_disabled`/`api.auth_enabled` reach the log and in-memory subscribers, not the persistent `EventStream`. A review suggested persisting transitions and bounded denial aggregates, failing closed if the audit write fails; that is a separate work item, not part of this PR.\n- **Follow-ups proposed by the review, deliberately not in this PR:** a `GovernanceKernel` decision before each control-plane side effect; removing inline script and handlers to enforce a strict CSP (the token is in `sessionStorage`); a second-account read test on Windows; the unrelated flaky updater test.\n- A same-user process can read the token file. `'unsafe-inline'` remains in the CSP, so an injected inline script can still read `sessionStorage`.\n- Not exercised: a real desktop `xdg-open`/Chrome/Firefox/Safari (the no-token-on-a-command-line property is tested with a stand-in launcher **plus a positive control** that proves the detector sees a leak), macOS, a frozen build on Windows/macOS, a genuinely separate host (an unprivileged uid in one container stood in), and the Windows cases listed above.\n- Unrelated and pre-existing: `tests/test_updater_error_disclosure.py` fails about 1 run in 2000 when a random UUID contains `8080`.\n- Dependabot PRs #92, #77, #30 bump pinned actions in `ci.yml`; they will not touch the new Windows job's pins, so bump them together.\n",
    "closed_by": null,
