    "body": "### Summary\n\nRepairs DEBT-012 by enforcing the requested module root and making test side effects an automated CI failure.\n\n### Changes\n\n- **Root-bound imports:** `load_all(modules_dir=...)` and `reload_module(..., modules_dir=...)` import the exact source under a private namespace derived from the canonical root, verify the loaded source and package paths, and do not edit `sys.path` or `modules.__path__`.\n- **Filesystem containment:** reject symlinked module directories and source files; reject source or package paths outside the requested root; require the class name to match its directory; reject existing symlinked BaseModule storage locations before constructor writes; verify the exact final storage root.\n- **Multi-root isolation:** retrieval cache keys include the canonical storage root and use a SHA-256 query digest, preventing same-named modules in different roots from sharing cached results or invalidation.\n- **Real isolation tests:** restore the two-root/stale-import-cache public API regression tests and storage/source symlink cases. Factory and security fixtures no longer force isolation by monkeypatching global roots or rewriting `modules.__path__`; repeat-cycle cleanup is protected by `finally`.\n- **Side-effect gate:** CI captures and verifies `config/`, `modules/`, `data/raw/`, and `data/chunks/` around pytest, including untracked/ignored files, symlinks and empty directories. The guard itself has focused tests.\n- **Tracked TOML:** remove the test-only `[test_config_reg_tmp]` residue while retaining the base file's original line-ending convention and unrelated content.\n- **Debt register:** DEBT-012 is active again until the exact current head passes CI and review. Earlier green runs refer to a superseded tree and are not used as closure evidence.\n\n### Scope boundary\n\nThe root parameter controls registry import resolution and BaseModule-managed storage; it is not a Python sandbox for arbitrary plugin code. The current generated module template still reads the process-wide config singleton, and training pairs intentionally use the shared `data/raw/<module>/` pipeline location. A fully isolated per-plugin configuration/data environment would require a separate `ModuleEnvironment` contract and is not represented as solved here.\n\n### Verification\n\nDo not merge until the latest exact-head CI run passes both the pytest gate and the protected-runtime-tree post-test verification. No merge has been performed.",
