      "merged_at": null
    },
    "body": "## Purpose\n\nPreserve the G4 FTS correctness REV3 decision state in the repository and provide a controlled resume point for a fresh session. This is a documentation-only checkpoint; it does not authorize implementation or ratify any ledger decision.\n\n## Included\n\n- A G4 continuation record with evidence limits, external artifact hashes, current-main reconciliation, D-1…D-11 status, and next-session order.\n- The proposed D-2/D-5 decision ledger, revised fetch-quotation header, and REV3 fresh-extraction verification report.\n- A fresh-session prompt that requires the original handoff and exact evidence ZIP to be attached and hash-checked.\n- One roadmap sync note.\n\n## Preserved outside Git by design\n\n- REV3 evidence ZIP: `fts_decision_packet_errata_evidence_1d813bd_D2_D5_FETCH_HEADER_REV3.zip`\n  - SHA-256: `f9ee626551e5175a7ba0893c336a77917b8be1b4078903cc6ac5853ad7e509cc`\n  - 254,581 bytes; 86 manifest entries; fresh-extraction check reported 86/86.\n- Original full handoff `handoff(1).md`\n  - SHA-256: `da162e71d6bd0b92650134eceb6af1ecfa430484ac08b179d7aaa48a97fa716d`\n  - Not copied into Git through a text-normalizing connector because its embedded original prompt was verified byte-identical and must remain byte-faithful. Attach the original file to a fresh session.\n\nThe external source documents are line-ending-normalized in the Git text copies; their recorded source-file hashes refer to the separately preserved delivered files / archive, not the Git blob hashes.\n\n## Scope and verification\n\n- No product code, tests, CI configuration, allowlists, xfails, migration code, runtime contract, or freeze state changed.\n- Live `main` was `f13bfdefcdd197ed1f966de0b1f93037a4168af4` when checked; this branch is one commit ahead and zero commits behind.\n- `sqlite_storage.py`, `knowledge_entry.py`, and `test_session4c_architecture.py` had identical blob SHAs at the three cited refs.\n- `CURRENT_STATE.md` and `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` are deliberately not changed here because multiple open PRs already edit those files. Reconcile them after that concurrent work is reconciled; do not introduce avoidable conflicts.\n\nAll decisions D-1…D-11 remain OPEN. G4 OPEN · High · freeze-blocking; G5–G8 HELD; freeze readiness NOT DECLARED. The 83/83 transcription result belongs to the prior run on the final packet text and was not rerun during this packaging pass.",
    "closed_by": null,
