    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "issue_field_values": [

    ],
    "type": null,
    "active_lock_reason": null,
    "draft": false,
    "pull_request": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pulls/88",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/88",
      "diff_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/88.diff",
      "patch_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/88.patch",
      "merged_at": null
    },
    "body": "## Docs: record the owner-directed response-path disposition (K4.2 pairing retained, C-plus selected for implementation)\n\n**Status:** ready for review; **not merged**. Documentation only — no code, test, configuration or contract change. ADR-KERNEL-07 stays **PROPOSED**; DEBT-042 and DEBT-043 stay **OPEN**; no freeze-readiness claim. Merging requires Moncif's explicit authorization through `premerge_guard.py` pinned to the head SHA.\n\n### What it records\n- **ADR §10.5 (new):** on 2026-10-19 — the date of the owner's remediation directive; no earlier decision is recorded — the owner **retained the K4.2 pairing requirement** for this response path (a detector-specific question only with a concrete, truthful representation of the interpreted intent *and* a genuine provisional plan) and selected containment option **C-plus** for implementation: at most three genuine plan steps, corrected formatting, an honest representation of the intent, an artifact-appropriate question. **A, B and D are not selected.**\n- **Provenance, stated explicitly:** C-plus extends historical candidate C; it was **not selected by the repeated-run experiment** and is **not part of the 2026-09-29 D-5 decision**, which is unchanged (no new gate; K4.2 not superseded). D-5 \"Option C\" and containment C/C-plus are kept distinct.\n- **Residual product risk:** C-plus reduces what is displayed; it does not establish that the remaining steps are semantically appropriate. A genuine planner step can still be generic, unsuitable or presuppose an unrequested process; the plan must be labeled provisional and is not verified.\n- **Historical passages qualified, not rewritten:** a dated status note in ADR §10.4 and in the result record marks the October 17 \"remaining owner decision\" sentence (and the earlier reading favoring B) as **historical and superseded for this response path**. The October 17 correction itself and all experimental evidence, thresholds, criteria and verdicts are untouched.\n- **`KNOWN_ISSUES.md`:** the DEBT-043 disposition no longer says the A–D choice is undecided; status stays **OPEN** (selected, not implemented or verified). **`CURRENT_STATE.md`:** a concise Oct 19 entry and the ADR-KERNEL-07 status row; earlier entries kept as history.\n\n### Live preflight (2026-10-19)\n- `main` = `f13bfdefcdd197ed1f966de0b1f93037a4168af4` (verified live, as expected); working tree clean; no existing branch or PR addresses DEBT-042/043.\n- **Open-PR overlaps** (11 open): #81 (DEBT-028 workflow fix, base `f13bfde`) edits `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` adjacent to the DEBT-043 row, so the two will conflict mechanically — whichever merges second needs a trivial update. #83 and #79 (base `488129b`) already conflict with current `main` on `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` since #82 merged, independent of this PR. #86 (stacked on a sandbox branch) and the Dependabot PRs do not touch these files. This PR touches no code.\n\n### Known gap (not hidden)\nThe owner's directive refers to a defined safe-failure response (its §5.4). The directive text I received ended inside §3.4, so that specification is **not** recorded here; ADR §10.5 records only the prohibition (no unpaired detector-specific question) and says the specification will be recorded when the DEBT-043 implementation lands.\n\n### Verification\n`check_drift.py` passes; runbook-validator tests pass; the new and qualified paragraphs were read in place; a scan of the added lines found no claim of freeze readiness, ADR acceptance or debt closure.\n",
    "closed_by": null,
