    "body": "## What\nTwo corrections to register rows that are mine (Packets C and G). Diff is exactly two lines.\n\n**`DEBT-033`** still described an admin exemption (`enforce_admins: false`, the owner's Sept 19 choice) and recorded \"admin-credentialed direct pushes\" as a residual. The live branch-protection API reports **`enforce_admins: true`** (PR #57 saw it on Oct 5; re-read Oct 16 and Oct 18), so that residual is closed in practice. Whether this was a deliberate revision of the earlier choice is not recorded, and the row says so rather than guessing.\n\n**`DEBT-030`** (`CapabilityRequest.trace_id` is a fresh random UUID — Packet C `C-1`) and **FZ-06** (identity not joinable across events, four namespaces) describe **one defect**, rediscovered independently by the Oct 1 audit. Neither row cited the other; `DEBT-030` now does, so it is counted once.\n\n## Deliberately not touched\n- The **FZ-06 row** — PR #83 edits the FZ block; editing it here would set two open PRs against each other. The cross-reference is discoverable from `DEBT-030`'s side.\n- The **CodeQL fixed-count** mismatch (docs say 34, the API lists 33) — cause unknown.\n- **`CURRENT_STATE.md`**'s unreconciled Sept 23 verdict wording — the owner's call.\n\n## Verification\nAll 34 `DEBT` rows present once before and after; drift 15/15; full suite 2072 passed / 1 xfailed. No code changed.\n\nContext: this is step 4 of the freeze-manifest draft's §10 (\"reconcile §6\"), items G3 and G5. No merge requested.",
    "closed_by": null,
