    "body": "**Owner:** @1h0lde4. **Status: exposure NOT established.** Separate from DEBT-032 / #65 (`chromadb`), from #62/#63, and from the registry PRs. Nothing here changes a dependency or dismisses an alert.\n\n## The alert (Dependabot #4, read from the API on `main` @ `73faf22`)\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Advisory | GHSA-jhr6-gm9c-rqjv / **CVE-2026-68770**, CWE-94, **critical, CVSS 9.8** (`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H`) |\n| Package | `sentence-transformers`, vulnerable `< 5.6.0`, first patched **5.6.0** |\n| Manifest / scope | `pyproject.toml`, runtime |\n| Published / updated / alert created | 2026-07-31 / 2026-09-30 / **2026-10-04** |\n| State | open (not dismissed) |\n\n## Mechanism, as stated by the advisory (not independently verified here)\n`import_module_class` (`sentence_transformers/util/misc.py`) has a guard containing `or os.path.exists(model_name_or_path)`, which satisfies the trust gate **whenever the supplied path exists on the local filesystem**, regardless of `trust_remote_code=False`. Anyone who can control or influence the contents of a **model directory on disk** can place Python files (e.g. `modeling_*.py` referenced via `modules.json`) that run at import time when `SentenceTransformer(path, trust_remote_code=False)` loads it.\nSo exposure needs **both**: (1) a model is loaded from a path that exists locally, and (2) an attacker can influence that directory's contents.\n\n## What is verified in this repo (on `main` @ `73faf22`)\n- Declared range **excludes the fix**: `pyproject.toml:46` and `requirements.txt:17` both say `sentence-transformers>=3.0.0,<4.0`. The patched `5.6.0` is unreachable without a major-version change (policy decision, not made here).\n- Three routes construct models: `core/learning/similarity.py:20` (literal `'all-MiniLM-L6-v2'`); `core/memory/backends/memory_vector.py:121` (`self._model_name`; its only non-test construction is `InMemoryVectorBackend()` with no argument at `core/memory/unified_memory.py:289`); `modules/embedding_fn.py:32` (name chosen from the fixed `_MODEL_MAP` at line 16).\n- No config key names an embedding model; no non-test caller passes a model name or path; no `trust_remote_code` anywhere in the repo.\n- `release.yml:195,203` mentions an Android APK build that includes `sentence-transformers` (a further deployment mode).\n\n## What is NOT established (the assessment must answer these)\n1. Do any of the three routes ever receive a name that **resolves as an existing local path** (e.g. the identifier happening to name a directory relative to the working directory), or does the library resolve hub names to a **local cache snapshot path** before the guard runs? Which is it in the pinned `3.x` versions actually installed?\n2. **Who can write** the directories models load from, in each supported deployment (local install, release builds, Android APK): the Hugging Face / sentence-transformers cache, any `modules/*` model directory, anything under the working directory?\n3. Is model download enabled at runtime, or offline-only? Can an attacker influence what is fetched or cached?\n4. Is the vulnerable code path reachable at all in `3.x` (the advisory range is `< 5.6.0`, but the guard's presence in `3.x` was not checked here)?\n\n## Decisions needed from the owner (after the assessment)\n- Exposure verdict (exposed / conditionally exposed / not exposed) with the evidence per deployment mode.\n- If action is warranted: the upgrade path (a `3.x` to `5.6.0+` major jump needs its own compatibility work), a documented mitigation, or a recorded boundary decision as done for `chromadb`.\n- Alert disposition policy: **do not dismiss #4** until the above is decided.\n\n## Constraints\n- Do not change dependencies or the declared range as part of the assessment.\n- Keep separate from #65 (that item is about a different package and a different mismatch).\n- The registry currently carries a \"noted, not yet assessed\" sentence (merged in #66); updating it to reference this item is a separate follow-up, after the assessment.\n\n## Acceptance\nA written exposure assessment with evidence for questions 1-4, the owner's decision recorded, and the alert's state left as the owner decides.\n",
