    "body": "**Owner:** @1h0lde4. Separate from the DEBT-032 security-boundary decision (embedded-only; recorded in the registry PR) and from PR #63.\n\n## Facts (verified on `main` @ `58d079f`)\n| Where | Declares | Used by |\n|---|---|---|\n| `requirements.txt:4` | `chromadb==0.5.3` | `ci.yml`: `pip install -r requirements.txt` |\n| `.github/workflows/release.yml:35,84,137` | `chromadb==0.5.3` (then also installs `requirements.txt`) | release builds |\n| `pyproject.toml:45` | `chromadb>=0.4.0,<1.0` | any pyproject-based install (`pip install .`, editable) |\n\nTested contract (DEBT-032, Sept 18-19, 2026): `0.5.3` reads the `modules/{mock,system_ctrl,empty_test}/knowledge` fixtures that fail under `0.6.3`. `requirements.txt` was tightened to `==0.5.3` on Sept 19 (Packet G Track 1); `pyproject.toml` was not. So a pyproject-based install can resolve to an incompatible release, because `0.6.3` is inside the declared range.\n\n## Why it matters\nThe package metadata does not state the supported version; the resolver is free to choose any `0.x` below `1.0`. Consumers of the metadata see a different contract than CI and the release pipeline.\n\n## Ask (a decision for the owner; nothing is implemented here)\nMake the declared constraint truthful so the supported version is explicit and not resolver-chosen. The form is the owner's call: an exact pin matching `requirements.txt`/`release.yml`, or a bounded range proven to exclude incompatible releases (DEBT-032 originally suggested `<0.6.0`); and whether `requirements.txt` or `pyproject.toml` is the single source of truth.\n\n## Constraints\n- Do not change dependency behavior or install anything as part of recording this item.\n- Do **not** dismiss Dependabot alerts #1-#3 (`chromadb`) until the declaration is truthful; dismissal is a deliberate policy decision afterwards.\n- Out of scope: the broader \"CI does not test the release dependency set\" debt (stays open under DEBT-032); the `sentence-transformers` alert #4 (separate).\n\n## Acceptance\n`pyproject.toml`, `requirements.txt` and `release.yml` agree on the supported `chromadb` version, and a check or test pins that agreement (form chosen by the owner).\n",
    "closed_by": null,
